WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:03.850
Too Many Crooks. A dice negotiation game where your score

2
00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:06.640
depends on the dice other players decide to send you.

3
00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:09.530
The whole game is about talking: bargaining,

4
00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:11.780
promising, and deciding who to trust.

5
00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:15.540
Every die is a crook, and its number says which kind.

6
00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:20.330
A job needs a crew, one of each kind of crook, and you score their total.

7
00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:24.010
The catch: you send four dice to your rivals.

8
00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:26.100
Your crew is whatever they send you.

9
00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:29.900
And their pay? Whatever dice you have left over.

10
00:00:30.470 --> 00:00:32.880
In this game, all deals are made out loud.

11
00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:36.550
Ruby, if you give me your six, I'll pay you six.

12
00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:38.700
She agrees and sends me her six.

13
00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:41.430
Moe makes her the same offer with two crooks.

14
00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:43.030
I send Ruby my six,

15
00:00:43.030 --> 00:00:45.010
and keep four dice to pay my crew.

16
00:00:45.510 --> 00:00:49.220
My crew: six and four and one. Eleven points.

17
00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:53.500
Then everyone pays their crew in secret, with all the dice they kept.

18
00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:58.340
My plan was to backstab Ruby all along, so I assign her crook a wage of one,

19
00:00:58.360 --> 00:01:00.760
giving her only one point instead of six.

20
00:01:00.890 --> 00:01:05.410
At the reveal, Ruby pays me nine. Moe gets nothing.

21
00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:09.150
Promises in this game aren't binding, but everyone saw it.

22
00:01:09.510 --> 00:01:13.210
Deciding who to cut out, and when to cut players out, is the core of the game.

23
00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:16.880
Go back on your word, and everybody becomes wary of making deals with you.

24
00:01:17.470 --> 00:01:18.850
The game plays in three rounds,

25
00:01:18.870 --> 00:01:22.530
and each round tests the trust that was built in previous rounds and games.

26
00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:25.670
Three to six players, and twenty or thirty minutes.

27
00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:27.830
Forty-eight dice and six player boards.

28
00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:30.380
The most points after three jobs wins.

29
00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:33.850
Too Many Crooks. Play it in your browser at darrendon.com,

30
00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:35.730
or email me for a prototype.

